# SIS Architecture — Mandatory Principles

**Precedence:** Subordinate only to `00-SIS-CONSTITUTION.mdc` and `.cursor/architecture/SIS-CONSTITUTION.md`.  
**Detailed rules:** `clean-architecture.mdc`, `architecture-governance.mdc`, `ARCHITECTURE-STACK.md`, path-scoped governance below.

```text
SIS Constitution → 01-ARCHITECTURE → sis-core → Clean Architecture / Architecture Governance
→ Module contracts → Security / Database / API / UI / Testing → Framework conventions → Laravel conventions
```

Framework conventions **never** override SIS architecture.

## Non-Negotiable Principles

1. **Domain/Application remain framework-independent** — no Illuminate, Eloquent, HTTP, or DB in Domain.
2. **Business logic must not live in UI** — React/Inertia/pages/hooks are presentation only.
3. **Controllers must not become business-logic containers** — delegate to Application handlers.
4. **Infrastructure boundaries must be respected** — persistence, queues, external IO in Infrastructure only.
5. **Authorization and tenant isolation are mandatory** — server-side on every protected operation.
6. **Database access follows database governance** — migrations only; see `database-changes-mandatory.mdc`.
7. **API contracts must be respected** — search consumers before breaking changes; see `08-api-governance.mdc`.
8. **UI must follow UI contracts** — `UI-CONTRACT.md`, `02-ui-ux.mdc`, `react-inertia.mdc`.
9. **New frameworks require architecture review** — ADR + human approval before introduction.
10. **Platform-specific behavior belongs only in platform/presentation adapters** — not Domain/Application.
11. **Business logic must never branch on OS/device/framework** — capability-based presentation only.
12. **Existing architecture validators and CI are mandatory** — `architecture:validate --fitness`, feature-check, graph.
13. **Conflicts must be resolved according to governance precedence** — see `GOVERNANCE-MAP.md`.
14. **Architecture violations require STOP before implementation** — read applicable rules and skills first.
15. **Inspect relevant detailed rules before changing architecture-sensitive code** — especially `app/**`, `resources/js/**`, `database/**`, `routes/**`.

## Before You Code (architecture-sensitive paths)

```text
.cursor/skills/application-feature/SKILL.md   (new features)
.cursor/architecture/ARCHITECTURE-STACK.md    (layer placement)
clean-architecture.mdc                        (app/**)
architecture-governance.mdc                   (app/**)
laravel-patterns.mdc                          (Infrastructure/Laravel glue only — subordinate)
```

## Validation (when touching application structure)

```bash
php artisan architecture:validate --fitness
php artisan architecture:feature-check {Context}   # when module changes
php artisan architecture:graph                     # dependency audit
```
